Two independent domain bugs causing silent revenue loss and a complete release-upload blockade in the Artist Portal.

## Bug 1 — Silent EUR zeroing in `convertToEur` (`src/lib/sos/currency.ts`)

When a currency had no rate entry (API outage, unmapped currency code), the function silently returned `0`, producing `0.00 EUR` royalty lines with no visible error. Artists would lose earnings for those sales without any indication.

**Fix:** throw instead of returning `0`, aborting statement generation and forcing the label to supply the missing rate before any statement is dispatched.

```ts
// Before — silent data loss
if (!rate || rate <= 0) {
  console.warn(`[currency] No exchange rate for ${code} — amount excluded from EUR totals`)
  return 0
}

// After — hard failure
if (!rate || rate <= 0) {
  throw new Error(
    `Missing exchange rate for currency "${code}" — add the rate before generating statements`,
  )
}
```

## Bug 2 — Custom required fields always failing in `submit-release` (`app/api/portal/submit-release/route.ts`)

The dynamic schema validation loop read every `submission_form_schema` field directly from the root `body` object. Standard fields happened to work because of a partial ternary mapping, but custom/admin-defined fields (e.g. "Producer Name") are sent inside `body.formData`. They were never found at the root level → always `undefined` → always HTTP 400, blocking every release upload that used any dynamic required field.

**Fix:** replace the ternary chain with a `STANDARD_FIELD_TO_BODY_KEY` map; any `fieldKey` absent from the map is treated as a custom field and looked up in `body.formData` instead.

```ts
const STANDARD_FIELD_TO_BODY_KEY: Record<string, string> = {
  title: 'title',
  audio_download_url: 'audioDownloadUrl',
  // … all 14 known standard fields
}

const bodyKey = STANDARD_FIELD_TO_BODY_KEY[field.fieldKey]
const val = bodyKey !== undefined
  ? (body as Record<string, unknown>)[bodyKey]
  : (body.formData ?? {})[field.fieldKey]   // ← custom fields now resolved correctly
```

